{
  // WHY THIS ONE FILE IS IN SOURCE CONTROL WHEN THE REST OF .vs/ IS NOT.
  //
  // Visual Studio opens this repository in Open Folder mode, and its Startup
  // Item dropdown is fed from two places. The first is the CMake file API, and
  // nothing in this repository can touch it -- the long note above
  // add_subdirectory(ThirdParty) in the root CMakeLists.txt says what was
  // measured. The second is Visual Studio's own scan of the folder tree, which
  // finds .sln and .vcxproj files and offers them whether or not this project
  // builds them. THIS FILE IS THE ONLY COMMITTED LEVER ON THAT SECOND HALF.
  //
  // The second half is entirely ThirdParty/GekkoNet. It is a PINNED SUBMODULE
  // (.gitmodules -> HeatXD/GekkoNet), it ships GekkoNet.sln, GekkoLib.vcxproj
  // and six Examples/*.vcxproj, and this build compiles none of them:
  // ThirdParty/CMakeLists.txt builds GekkoLib/src/*.cpp with OUR flags
  // precisely because the upstream project files force /MT against our /MD.
  // They are upstream files at a pinned commit, so deleting them is not on the
  // table; keeping Visual Studio from scanning them is.
  //
  // .gitignore was changed from `.vs/` to `.vs/*` plus one negation to allow
  // this. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so
  // the shorter form would have made the exception silently inert. Everything
  // else Visual Studio writes here is still per-user and still ignored.
  //
  // GekkoLib/src IS DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED. We compile it, so search and Go
  // To Definition have to keep reaching it. Only the project FILES and the
  // Examples tree go, because only those become IDE entries.
  //
  // IF VISUAL STUDIO EVER REWRITES THIS FILE -- it owns the name, and a
  // settings change made through the IDE can land here -- the fix is to put the
  // three GekkoNet entries back. That is also the whole of the per-user step for
  // anyone whose Visual Studio ignores the file: the mechanism is per-user by
  // design, and committing it only means every clone starts with it applied.
  "ExcludedItems": [
    // Visual Studio's own defaults, repeated on purpose. This file may REPLACE
    // the default array rather than merge with it, and quietly losing the .git
    // exclusion would be a far worse trade than any GekkoNet entry is worth.
    ".git",
    ".vs",
    ".vscode",
    "node_modules/",

    // The pinned submodule's own Visual Studio projects: not ours, not built by
    // us, and the entire content of "why does the dropdown list six sessions I
    // have never heard of".
    "ThirdParty/GekkoNet/GekkoNet.sln",
    "ThirdParty/GekkoNet/GekkoLib/GekkoLib.vcxproj",
    "ThirdParty/GekkoNet/Examples/"
  ]
}
